Falsifies `inter_process_communication::notification::verification::a_wait_returns_a_nonzero_word_or_blocks`.

The defect: `WAIT` reads the word and forgets to clear it, so the same bits are delivered again
on every later wait. A copy where a take was meant.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(n.word, 0)` after `Wait::Word`.

diff --git a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/notification.rs b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/notification.rs
index c20bff922..d70bab7a0 100644
--- a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/notification.rs
+++ b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/notification.rs
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ impl<T: Node> Notification<T> {
     /// `Blocked`, which the reaper never frees).
     pub unsafe fn wait(&mut self, me: NonNull<T>) -> Wait {
         if self.word != 0 {
-            Wait::Word(core::mem::take(&mut self.word))
+            Wait::Word(self.word)
         } else {
             // SAFETY: the caller's contract is exactly the queue's.
             unsafe { self.waiters.push_back(me) };
